"""Hand-written card bodies for the eighteen technique cards.

Keys are (card_name, field_name) pairs matching ``lc_review.elements.CARDS``
and ``lc_review.elements.FIELDS``. Values for the first five fields are
Chinese prose written from the labuladong source articles cited on each
card (see ``ElementCard.sources``) -- summarized or closely paraphrased from
the fetched article text, not invented. Where an article genuinely does not
address a field, the value is the literal string 原文未涉及 rather than a
guess.

The 典型坑 field is different: it is assembled mechanically from echo's own
orange-highlighted retrospective notes in review_state.json (`我的复盘.高亮`),
grouped by the 要素卡 each record was linked to by
``lc_review.elements.link_state_to_cards``. Each entry lists the source
problem id/title followed by her highlights, quoted verbatim -- nothing here
is paraphrased or added. A card with no highlighted retrospectives simply has
no 典型坑 entry, so ``render_elements`` falls back to 待填写 for it rather
than a fabricated pitfall.
"""

